Rename sed's global 'debug' flag to 'sed_debug'.

libphoenix exports an un-namespaced global 'debug' (the Phoenix
kernel debug-console syscall wrapper, libphoenix
arch/aarch64/syscalls.S). Linking sed statically against libc.a
therefore fails with:
  libc.a(syscalls.o): in function 'debug':
  multiple definition of 'debug'; sed/sed-sed.o:(.bss.debug+0x0)
Renaming the sed-side variable is the least invasive fix; the
user-visible --debug option is a string literal and unaffected.

